    "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-4\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-x(-4-3\\text{i})-x(-4+3\\text{i})+(-4+3\\text{i})(-4-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}+8x+25) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+25x-3{x}^{2}-24x-75 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75.$",
